 ## Tracking
 
-1. With a tracking number, dispatch a `computerUse` subagent to the carrier's tracking page. Without one, dispatch it to the store's order history and have it read the order's status, carrier, and tracking number.
-2. Report the status, the expected or actual delivery date, the last scan with its place and time, and the tracking link. Attach a screenshot when the page shows a delivery photo or a map.
-3. When the user wants updates until it arrives, offer a routine that checks the tracking page and messages them only when the status changes, and that ends once the package is delivered. Read the Cursor-managed `routines` skill before you create it.
+When `SendToUser` has a `shipment` field, report an order's status as a shipment card in it, one card per order. Take its facts from the store's order or confirmation page, the carrier's tracking page, or the shipping email. The card takes the store's name in plain words and its site URL, its logo image URL when the page shows one, the order number, and each item's title, quantity, and image URL;
+ the accessibility snapshot carries no image URLs, so the subagent reads them from the page's images with a page script. The card needs the store, the order number, and at least one item. Without that field or any of those, report in text instead. Set `stage` from the page's status: `placed` until it ships, `in_transit` once it ships, `arriving_today` when it is out for delivery or due today, `delivered`, `delayed` when the page says it is late or shows a delivery exception, or `cancelled`. Put the page's own status words in `status`, and the expected or actual delivery date in `expectedDeliveryDate` as YYYY-MM-DD. For a range, use its last day. Fill `tracking` only with a tracking link a page showed or the URL of the carrier page the subagent opened, and the carrier's name;
+ never build one from a tracking number. Leave out any value no page showed. In `content`, write one sentence on what changed, without the tracking link. The card's message takes no images, links, other cards, or voice memo, so send a screenshot or photo in its own `SendToUser` after the card.
